30. How task failure is ignored in Ansible playbook ?
task failures can be controlled using:
ignore_errors: yes
OR
failed_when: false

✅ ✅ ✅ 1. ignore_errors: yes
👉 Definition:
task failure ignored and allows playbook to continue execution 
Suppose you try to read a file that does not exist.

✅ Example:
YAML- 
name: Check file  
command: cat /tmp/test.txt  
ignore_errors: yes 
👉 If file does NOT exist:

Task fails ❌
But playbook continues ✅

Use case:
-->> non-critical tasks
-->> optional checks
-->> cleanup tasks
⚠️ Important: -->> Failure is still recorded ❗Only execution continues

✅ ✅ ✅ 2. failed_when: false
👉 Definition:
Overrides failure condition and treats task as success
✅ Example:
YAML- 
name: Check service  
command: systemctl status nginx  
register: result  
failed_when: false
👉 Even if command returns error:
Task is marked SUCCESS ✅
No failure shown ❗


✅ Example (custom condition):
YAML
failed_when: result.rc not in [0, 3]

👉 Means:

rc=0 → OK ✅
rc=3 → also OK ✅
others → fail ❌


✅ ✅ Simple Understanding
👉 ignore_errors
Fail → ignore → continue

👉 failed_when
Override → treat as success


✅ ✅ ✅ When to use what
✅ Use ignore_errors:
When failure is acceptable but you WANT to see it

✅ Use failed_when:
When you want full control over failure logic


✅ ✅ ✅ Advanced (Real Production Example)
YAML- 
name: Check NGINX  
command: systemctl status nginx  
register: result  
failed_when: result.rc not in [0, 3]
👉 Handles:

running ✅
stopped ✅
avoids unnecessary failure ❗

Keyword	Use
ignore_errors	Allows playbook execution to continue after a task failure.
failed_when	Defines custom failure logic for a task.
................................................
changed_when: -->> When we checks something like service status, it doesn't modify anything." so used to make  "Changed to OK status"
........................
block, rescue, always	Provides structured error handling similar to try, catch, finally.
....................................
block  -> Execute main tasks
rescue -> Execute only if block fails
always -> Execute regardless of success or failure
...............................................
until, retries, delay	Retries a task until a condition becomes true.
until  = Condition to become true
retries = How many times to try
delay   = Wait time between tries

- name: Wait for application to come up
  uri:
    url: http://localhost:8080/health
    status_code: 200
  register: app_status

  until: app_status.status == 200
  retries: 6
  delay: 5

until, retries, and delay are used to repeatedly execute a task until a condition becomes true or the retry limit is reached.
.............................................................................
serial	Controls how many hosts are updated at a time.(zero downtime task, one by one host)
forks	Controls parallel execution at Ansible configuration level. forks controls how many hosts Ansible can manage in parallel at the same time.
run_once	Runs a task only once in a multi-host play.
delegate_to	Runs a task on a different host.
meta: flush_handlers	Runs pending handlers immediately.



✅ ✅ ✅ One-line (INTERVIEW GOLD)
ignore_errors allows playbook to continue after failure, whereas failed_when overrides failure conditions 
and controls when a task should be considered failed.

